"""
Internal administrative-boundary overlay (raion/"district") lines for all
25 oblasts that are subdivided into raions under the 2020 reform, plus
Kyiv City and Sevastopol -- see the note at the bottom of this docstring
for why those two have no entries here. Display-only: this data never
affects region hit-testing, alert state, risk scoring, or any other
non-visual behavior -- only what gets drawn as a light internal-border
overlay when an oblast is focused/zoomed into on the Ukraine map.

Source: slawomirmatuszak/ukrainian_geodata (rayony.geojson -- Ukraine's
136 post-2020-reform raions), free and open, licensed CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/):
https://github.com/slawomirmatuszak/ukrainian_geodata

Each raion's owning oblast was verified empirically (its centroid tested
against this project's own ``region_at_point``/``REGION_RINGS``, with a
nearest-polygon-edge fallback for the one raion -- Izmail, in Odesa
Oblast -- whose centroid landed just outside every oblast polygon due to
its position on the simplified Odesa coastline), not assumed from name
alone. All 136 raions resolved successfully.

Coordinates are projected into this project's shared SVG viewBox space
with ``app.ukraine_geo.project_lat_lon`` (same projection as
``REGION_RINGS`` and the region-border rendering already on this map),
and simplified with Douglas-Peucker (epsilon=0.6 viewBox units, matching
the pipeline previously used for the Kyiv/Cherkasy-only version of this
file) to cut point count roughly 4-5x for smooth mobile rendering while
keeping each raion's shape recognizable -- these are meant to be read as
a light internal-border overlay, not a survey-grade boundary.

NOT COVERED -- missing source data, not an oversight:
  * Kyiv City (``Region.KYIV_CITY``) has its own internal city-district
    system (e.g. Pecherskyi, Solomianskyi raions), which is a DIFFERENT
    administrative category than the oblast-subdivision "rayony" this
    source covers, and isn't present in rayony.geojson at all.
  * Sevastopol (``Region.SEVASTOPOL``) is not present in rayony.geojson
    either (the 2020 reform this dataset reflects did not cover it).
No placeholder/invented geometry has been added for either -- the Ukraine
map still renders both regions' own oblast-level border correctly via
``REGION_RINGS``; only this raion overlay is unavailable for them.
"""

